      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">Bab al-Mandab Strait</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Airlines and Airplanes</category>
      <ns1:content height="1801" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/11/multimedia/11int-saudi-assess-bvtm/11int-saudi-assess-bvtm-mediumSquareAt3X-v2.jpg" width="1800" />
      <ns1:credit>Pool photo by Julie Sebadelha</ns1:credit>
      <ns1:description>Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman of Saudi Arabia in Paris in August. Houthi strikes on the Saudi capital, Riyadh, have cast a shadow on his efforts to transform the kingdom into a global hub for business and tourism.</ns1:description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>India’s ‘Cockroach’ Leaders Released as Small Protests Go On in Delhi</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/11/world/asia/india-cockroach-dipke-new-delhi-protests.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/11/world/asia/india-cockroach-dipke-new-delhi-protests.html</guid>
      <ns0:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/11/world/asia/india-cockroach-dipke-new-delhi-protests.html" rel="standout" />
      <description>The leaders of the Cockroach Janta Party, an Indian youth movement, had been detained by the police on Saturday before they could lead protests over voting rights.</description>
      <pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:16:44 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">India</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_org">Cockroach Janta Party (India)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Demonstrations, Protests and Riots</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Political Prisoners</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_geo">New Delhi (India)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Youth</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Dipke, Abhijeet</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Politics and Government</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Voting Rights, Registration and Requirements</category>
      <ns1:content height="1800" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/11/multimedia/11int-india-protests-hjkb/11int-india-protests-hjkb-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800" />
      <ns1:credit>Saumya Khandelwal for The New York Times</ns1:credit>
      <ns1:description>Ratna Singh, the legal director of the Cockroach Janta Party, left, with Ashutosh Ranka and Saurav Das, two of the group’s leaders, at the Press Club of India in New Delhi on Saturday.</ns1:description>
    </item>
    <item>
